# chromadb 1.5.9 pre-auth RCE (server/services/python/requirements.txt).
# Pre-existing pin surfaced now that Trivy scanning is blocking. No patched
# chromadb release is published for this CVE yet (Trivy reports no fixed
# version), so it cannot be remediated by a version bump. Allowlisted to keep
# the Trivy gate blocking for *fixable* CRITICAL/HIGH findings.
# TODO(security): upgrade chromadb as soon as a patched release ships, and
# confirm chromadb is not exposed to untrusted pre-auth network input.
CVE-2026-45829

# react-router GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (RSC-mode CSRF: an action can run before a
# 400 response). Range >=7.12.0 <8.3.0; the only fix is the react-router 8.x
# major. This app routes with wouter and uses react-router-dom only on a couple
# of auth screens — no RSC / data-router server actions — so the RSC CSRF path
# is not reachable. Trivy scans package-lock.json separately from npm audit, so
# this must be listed here in ADDITION to ACCEPTED_GHSA_IDS in
# scripts/ci/audit-with-allowlist.mjs. The other react-router advisory (route-
# matching DoS) is genuinely fixed by the react-router-dom 7.18.1 bump.
# TODO(security): adopt react-router 8.x in a dedicated upgrade PR, then drop this.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
